{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888570,"nonce":"zbga0IRFQvG5+5NCZii5r55RoUg=","title":"A Correlator cannot make its Incidents a conversation, so a storm it has already recognised still opens one Slack thread per Case","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0052 §6: per Correlator, an operator may say its Incidents are conversations; `conversation_kind` gains `incident` and later facts about member Cases post into the Incident's thread. `ConversationKind` has two values (`internal/notification/domain/notification.go:402,406`) and `threads_subjkind_ck` admits no `incident`.\n\n**The demonstration.** Forty Cases matched by one Correlator post forty root cards today, per ADR 0045.\n\n**Why it matters.** This is the narrowing of 0045 the owner ruled for.\n\n**Where.** A boolean on the Correlator; `notifications_convkind_ck` and `threads_subjkind_ck` (widened here, not in `aa6d18b`); the conversation selection in the notification layer, which reads the Case's Incident membership **when a fact is enqueued**, not when the Case opened; an Incident root card (members, active/quiet, outbound link) in the Slack renderer and both golden corpora (two update flags, two fixture URLs).\n\n**Scope.** medium.\n\n**Done when.** With the flag on, facts enqueued after the Case's membership exists post into the Incident thread with no new root, and facts enqueued before it stay in the Case's own thread — the boundary is the membership row's commit, so there is no race to test around; each Case that already had its own thread gets one \"now part of Incident #N →\" reply; nothing already posted moves; no fact is held back waiting for a Correlator; a human-drawn or moved membership redirects only later facts; ADR 0045 carries the narrowing note; both Slack golden corpora updated.\n\n**Blocked by.** `61eeddf`, `aa6d18b`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}